rem Message Manager trusts the certificates in the Windows certificate store (see JVM_OPTS in launch.cmd).

rem Message Manager downloads its own current Java after its first starts (about 100 MB) and switches to it once it has
rem passed its checks. Until then, and whenever it cannot be used, it runs on the Java it found before (the installer's
rem own, JAVA_HOME or java on the PATH): that one needs Java 17 or later.

rem OPTIONAL - if you want to override the default JVM options
rem set JVM_OPTS=-Djavax.net.ssl.trustStore=NUL -Djavax.net.ssl.trustStoreType=Windows-ROOT -Djava.net.useSystemProxies=true -Djavafx.embed.singleThread=true -Dswing.systemlaf=com.sun.java.swing.plaf.windows.WindowsLookAndFeel -DSolace_JMS_Browser_Timeout_In_MS=1000

rem Use LAUNCHER_JAVA to specify the Java executable to use; it wins over Message Manager's own Java
rem set LAUNCHER_JAVA=%JAVA_HOME%\bin\java.exe